[3] EXACT edge-isoperimetric profile + Cheeger (n=4,5)
    n=4: M(k) max-internal-edges = [0, 1, 3]
          b(k) min-edge-boundary   = [2, 3, 2]
          Cheeger edge-expansion h=min b(k)/k (k<=V/2) = 1.500   min-conductance phi = 0.600
          sparsest cut: A[|.|=2 SC=1 NS=1 H in [1,3]] | B[|.|=2 SC=1 NS=1 H in [3,5]]  ->  H-interval? False   SC-vs-NS? False
    n=5: M(k) max-internal-edges = [0, 1, 3, 6, 9, 13, 16, 19, 22, 25, 28]
          b(k) min-edge-boundary   = [2, 5, 7, 9, 11, 11, 11, 9, 7, 5, 2]
          Cheeger edge-expansion h=min b(k)/k (k<=V/2) = 1.833   min-conductance phi = 0.379
          sparsest cut: A[|.|=6 SC=4 NS=2 H in [1,15]] | B[|.|=6 SC=4 NS=2 H in [3,15]]  ->  H-interval? False   SC-vs-NS? False
    => sparsest cut is a BALANCED bisection spanning the full H-range and mixing SC/NS:
       the H-gradient / principal line is a GRADIENT, not a bottleneck.

[4] SPINE(SC-SC) / RIBS(SC-NS) / SEA(NS-NS) decomposition & induced dimension
    n=4: spine(SC-SC)=1 ribs(SC-NS)=4 sea(NS-NS)=0 | spine: 2 nodes/1 edges maxdeg=1 cyclomatic=0 ~QUASI-1D (path/tree)
    n=5: spine(SC-SC)=12 ribs(SC-NS)=16 sea(NS-NS)=2 | spine: 8 nodes/12 edges maxdeg=4 cyclomatic=5 branched
          SEA(NS-NS) as its own graph: 4 nodes, avgdeg=1.00, lam2(L)=0.000, normgap=0.0000  (sparse)
    n=6: spine(SC-SC)=13 ribs(SC-NS)=90 sea(NS-NS)=187 | spine: 12 nodes/13 edges maxdeg=3 cyclomatic=2 ~QUASI-1D (path/tree)
          SEA(NS-NS) as its own graph: 44 nodes, avgdeg=8.50, lam2(L)=1.980, normgap=0.3495  (expander core)

[5] VERDICT
    honeycomb A263135 : isoperimetric dim D=2, boundary ~ sqrt(N), diam ~ sqrt(N)  [AMENABLE]
    tournament G_n    : lam2(L)~2 (const) => boundary ~ Theta(V) at balanced cuts;
                        diam ~ log(V); sparsest cut transverse to H & SC/NS  [SMALL-WORLD, D=inf]
    The SEED sequence and the project's central object are ISOPERIMETRIC ANTIPODES.
    Internal structure spans the dimension axis: SPINE(SC) quasi-1D thread; SEA(NS) expander core.
